# This repository is a historical archive: every file must round-trip
# byte-for-byte. Disable ALL end-of-line conversion.
#
# Why it matters here:
#   - PLINKC.asm is Shift-JIS with CR-ONLY line endings (the A62 assembler
#     requires them); any CRLF/LF normalization would corrupt it.
#   - README.DOC / APLINKS.DOC / PLINKC.DOC carry their own encodings
#     (UTF-8 or Shift-JIS) with CRLF.
#   - PLINKC.OBJ and the .exe/.dll files are binaries.
* -text
